# HOSSPI HMS — Monorepo Rules Index

Purpose: single entry point for all Cursor rules in this repository.

## Product

**HOSSPI HMS** (HOSSPI Hospital Management System) is a full-stack, multi-tenant hospital management system:
- `frontend/` — Flutter client (`hosspi_hms`)
- `backend/` — Express.js API (`hms-backend`)
- Product scope and modules: [`app-write-up.mdc`](./app-write-up.mdc)

## Locale rule (contextual)

[`locale-development.mdc`](./locale-development.mdc) — during routine development, edit only English locale files (`app_en.arb`, `en.json`). Update French or other locale files only when the user explicitly requests it. Not always-applied; attaches via its globs.

## Conflict order

When rules disagree, apply this order:

1. Security, privacy, safety, and compliance
2. [`.cursor/api-contract.mdc`](./api-contract.mdc) for cross-stack HTTP, errors, pagination, and naming
3. Product scope in [`app-write-up.mdc`](./app-write-up.mdc)
4. Access defaults in [`.cursor/access/`](./access/)
5. Contextual flow files in [`.cursor/flows/`](./flows/) when editing those domains (see table below)
6. Stack owner index: [`frontend/.cursor/index.mdc`](../frontend/.cursor/index.mdc) or [`backend/.cursor/index.mdc`](../backend/.cursor/index.mdc)
7. Other stack-specific rule files named in the stack index
8. `dev-plan/` steps (chronology only — not a duplicate standards source)

For UI mutation and reconciliation behavior specifically,
[`frontend/.cursor/instant_ui_sync.mdc`](../frontend/.cursor/instant_ui_sync.mdc)
and [`frontend/.cursor/realtime_sync.mdc`](../frontend/.cursor/realtime_sync.mdc)
specialize the transport contract in `api-contract.mdc`.

## Access control defaults (source of truth)

| File | Owns |
|---|---|
| [`access/modules.mdc`](./access/modules.mdc) | Module catalog + default permissions per module |
| [`access/permissions.mdc`](./access/permissions.mdc) | Permission vocabulary, RBAC+ABAC matrix |
| [`access/subscriptions.mdc`](./access/subscriptions.mdc) | Package → module → permission enumeration |
| [`access/default_user_roles.mdc`](./access/default_user_roles.mdc) | Default roles → module permissions |

Effective access = union(role/module/user grants) ∩ active subscription ∩ ABAC scope. Admins may customize; all changes are atomic, auditable, and resettable to shipped defaults. No user may retain access beyond that intersection.

