## Cross-stack invariants

- API JSON, query params, and documented payload fields use lowercase `snake_case` (backend owns; frontend DTOs map explicitly).
- Success responses: `{ success: true, data, meta? }`; errors: normalized problem-details shape (see `api-contract.mdc`).
- Frontend must reference entities by `human_friendly_id`; backend maps to internal IDs. Do not expose raw table IDs in frontend or API responses.
- Backend authorization (RBAC, ABAC, subscription intersection, break-glass) is the source of truth; frontend mirrors it in guards and UI visibility.
- Offline-capable mutations are idempotent; auth, payments, break-glass, and mortuary release are online-only (see `api-contract.mdc`).
- CRUD mutations use HTTP; WebSocket delivers post-persistence domain events for multi-client UI refresh (see `api-contract.mdc`, `frontend/.cursor/realtime_sync.mdc`).
- UI reads only from Riverpod; mutations patch provider state optimistically on success; WebSockets reconcile Riverpod — never update widgets directly (see `frontend/.cursor/instant_ui_sync.mdc`).
